  "_description": "Machine-checked client-to-backend endpoint contract (ADR 0497 D5). Every entry below has a MEASURED call site in lib/** -- this is not a wishlist, per the round brief SS0.0 R6. Re-measured in full by R16 (2026-09-07, branch claude/mit-audit-javitasok-v432t5 @ 3d2f0e3) with `grep -rnE \"_client\\.(getJson|postJson|putJson|patchJson|post|delete)(<[^(]*>)?\\(\" lib`: 65 ApiClient call sites plus the three raw-Dio ones (auth token posts share one helper; the two /tutor + one /diagnostics call sites use Dio directly), collapsing to 67 distinct method+path pairs. R14 reported ~24 of them missing; the measured figure was 26, and all 26 are added here. `source` is the line carrying the endpoint path literal, except where the path is assembled into a local variable shared by more than one verb (post/comment reactions, bookmarks) -- there it is the line of the issuing call. `backend/tests/test_client_contract_parity.py` asserts every `status: mounted` entry's path+method exists in `app.openapi()['paths']`, and asserts every `status: known_gap` entry is ABSENT (a canary: if a future round implements it, that assertion breaks and forces this file to be updated to `mounted`). Javito sav R27 (2026-09-08): three MEASURED community-media call sites added -- POST /community/media (HttpCommunityPostRepository.uploadMedia, the tree's only multipart request), GET /community/media/{public_id} (communityMediaBytesProvider, the tree's only byte-body response) and DELETE /community/media/{public_id} (HttpCommunityPostRepository.deleteMedia). All three are `mounted`: test_client_contract_parity.py builds the app with community_media_enabled=true, and the router is registered under exactly that flag. 67 -> 70 entries. Javito sav R34 (2026-09-08, audit MI-M): the `source` LINE NUMBERS were re-measured against the working tree and 22 of the 70 entries were corrected -- the paths and the call sites were all still present, only the line numbers had drifted as the files grew (the audit reported four; the measured figure is 22). Rule used, unchanged from R16: `source` is the line carrying the endpoint path literal, except for the multi-verb shared path variables (post/comment reactions, bookmarks) where it is the line of the issuing call. WARNING: post_repository_impl.dart was under concurrent edit while this was measured, so its entries must be re-measured once that work lands. Nothing here is machine-checked yet -- backend/tests/test_client_contract_parity.py asserts `source` is non-empty and never that it points at the call site, which is why this drift went unnoticed for four rounds.",
